## The One Rule

**Don't overdo the gamification.**
If reading an email requires too many interactions or animations, we lose the "works just as good as Proton" goal.
The boba metaphor stays *visual and occasional,* never *structural.*

---

## Why This Theme Works

| Principle        | Reasoning                                                              |
|:-----------------|:-----------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **Anti-Anxiety** | Boba is inherently a "slow down" activity. It visually communicates "take your time." |
| **Inclusive**    | Appeals to the huge segment of gamers who prefer cozy/casual games, not just FPS/RPGs. |
| **Neutral**      | "Cute" is non-threatening. It removes any perceived aggression from the UI. |
| **Gamer-Coded**  | "Kawaii" and "Boba" are massive subcultures within gaming (VTubers, cozy streamers, etc.). |

